  ot-tools-sync sync [--sha SHA]   materialize main@SHA (default: origin/main) as the read-only versioned tree
                                   RT/<sha12> (a detached sparse worktree of the queue clone on the hub; tools/ +
                                   physical/common_flow, the same set as the old kw38/rt), smoke-test it, then flip the
                                   symlink RT/current to it with one rename.  The same version is copied (rsync, hard links
                                   to the previous version) to RT/<sha12> on every fleet host (OT_RT_HOSTS) and that host's
                                   RT/current is flipped after its own smoke test.  A version dir is never modified after
                                   it is made; running stages keep the dir they resolved (Path(__file__).resolve()).
  ot-tools-sync drift [--post]     live-only check: every file of RT/current (hub and hosts) against the version's manifest,
                                   the hub tree against git, the legacy kw38/rt tree against its own HEAD while a unit still
                                   runs it, and each host's active ot-run backend against tools/fleet/ot-run of RT/current.
                                   --post appends DRIFT lines to the review queue when the drift set changes.
  ot-tools-sync follow             (1-2 min timer, OWNER 11-18) fetch origin/main; when it moved and RT/current is an ancestor of it, run `sync`
                                   (fast-forward only: a main that does not contain RT/current is logged and skipped); no-op otherwise.
  ot-tools-sync status             current version per host.
Called by ot-merge-queue after every push to main (MQ_SYNC_HOOK).  Log: ~/merge-queue/log (prefix SYNC).
"""
